n-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Di Vincenzo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Meticulous prevention of hypoglycemia normalizes the glycemic thresholds and magnitude of most of neuroendocrine responses to, symptoms of, and cognitive function during hypoglycemia in intensively treated patients with short-term IDDM</article-title><source>Diabetes</source><volume>42</volume><fpage>1683</fpage><lpage>1689</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8405713</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b007"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Gabriely</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Shamoon</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Fructose normalizes specific counterregulatory responses to hypoglycemia in patients with type 1 diabetes</article-title><source>Diabetes</source><volume>54</volume><fpage>609</fpage><lpage>616</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15734834</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b008"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Gabriely</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Wozniak</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hawkins</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Shamoon</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Troglitazone amplifies counterregulatory responses to hypoglycemia in nondiabetic subjects</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><volume>86</volume><fpage>521</fpage><lpage>528</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11158003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b009"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Caprio</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerety</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamborlane</surname><given-names>WV</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Diamond</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Opiate blockade enhances hypoglycemic counterregulation in normal and insulin-dependent diabetic subjects</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><volume>260</volume><issue>Pt 1</issue><fpage>E852</fpage><lpage>E858</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2058661</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b010"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Chase</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Nocturnal hypoglycemia&#x02014;An unrelenting problem</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><volume>91</volume><fpage>2038</fpage><lpage>2039</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16757532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b011"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Cryer</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Mechanisms of hypoglycemia-associated autonomic failure and its component syndromes in diabetes</article-title><source>Diabetes</source><volume>54</volume><fpage>3592</fpage><lpage>3601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16306382</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Weston</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gill</surname><given-names>GV</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Is undetected autonomic dysfunction responsible for sudden death in type 1 diabetes mellitus? The &#x0201c;dead in bed&#x0201d; syndrome revisited</article-title><source>Diabet Med</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>626</fpage><lpage>631</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10477206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b013"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Porter</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherwin</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Leary</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Decreased epinephrine responses to hypoglycemia during sleep</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>338</volume><fpage>1657</fpage><lpage>1662</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Banarer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cryer</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Sleep-related hypoglycemia-associated autonomic failure in type 1 diabetes: Reduced awakening from sleep during hypoglycemia</article-title><source>Diabetes</source><volume>52</volume><fpage>1195</fpage><lpage>1203</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12716752</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b015"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Schultes</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Jauch-Chara</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Gais</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallschmid</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Reiprich</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Defective awakening response to nocturnal hypoglycemia in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>e69</fpage><comment>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.pmed.0040069">10.1371/journal.pmed.0040069</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17326710</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040099-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Bolli</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Treatment and prevention of hypoglycemia and its unawareness in type 1 diabetes mellitus</article-title><source>Rev Endocr Metab Disord</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>335</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14618018</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="n3" fn-type="current-aff"><p>Ilan Gabriely is Assistant Professor of Medicine, Department of Medicine and Diabetes Research Center, and Harry Shamoon is Professor of Medicine, Division of Endocrinology, and Associate Dean for Clinical Research and Program Director of the General Clinical Research Center, Albert Einstein College of Medicine, Bronx, New York.</p></fn><fn id="n1" fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> Supported in part by the following National Institutes of Health grants: DK62463 (HS), DK20541 (HS), RR017313 (IG), and M01-RR12248.</p></fn><fn id="n2" fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests:</bold> The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>